<h2>Open Source</h2>
<p>This platform is open source (MIT License). The election data is structured separately from the presentation code, so other communities can reuse it for their own elections.</p>
<p><a href="https://github.com/GoryGrey/OpenVoterGuide">View the OpenVoterGuide repository</a></p>

<h2>Privacy</h2>
<p>The voting worksheet saves your choices only in your browser's local storage. Nothing is sent to any server. There are no accounts, no tracking, and no analytics.</p>

<h2>Corrections</h2>
<p>Found an error? <a href="https://github.com/GoryGrey/OpenVoterGuide/issues/new">open a correction issue on GitHub</a> or email the maintainer. Corrections are published promptly with a changelog entry.</p>
